# The host-TU lint: the graph's `//csrc/rola:clang_tidy_host` runs it (`tools/lint/unit_lints.py`), with the PINNED
# clang-tidy (tools/clang_tidy_pin.json), on every `.cpp` the library links (today csrc/rola/rola_api.cpp). The device units have their own profile,
# tools/lint/clang-tidy-device.yaml. Every finding fails the gate (WarningsAsErrors).
#
# The check set is deliberately narrow: bugprone (real correctness classes)
# plus a small readability set, with nothing opinionated about naming or
# braces (this codebase's own style rules -- KERNEL_STANDARDS.md, the
# comments-to-docs mandate -- already govern that, and a second, disagreeing
# style opinion here would just be noise a contributor learns to ignore).
#
# Two exclusions carry their reason: `bugprone-throwing-static-initialization` fires on torch's op registration
# (STABLE_TORCH_LIBRARY), which is a static initializer by design; and `PyInit__C` is the name the Python
# C-extension ABI requires for the module `_C`, so the reserved-identifier check allows it by name.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-redundant-declaration,
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr,
  readability-container-size-empty

WarningsAsErrors: '*'
CheckOptions:
  bugprone-reserved-identifier.AllowedIdentifiers: 'PyInit__C'
HeaderFilterRegex: ''
FormatStyle: none
